      "content": "okay, but it feels like those original arguments are kinda weak or just focus on legal technicalities. like, isn't the whole point that the systemic wealth gap is a direct result of those historical wrongs? do people actually have better or more logically sound reasons than just \"it wasn't them personally\"?",
